    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe single create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`) is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. The incoming email is already trimmed and lower-cased there (with a syntactic validation step). I added a duplicate-email rejection alongside the existing conflict checks (telephone, household, city cap):\n\n- In `addOwner`, right after the telephone-in-use check:\n  ```java\n  if (owner.getEmail() != null && isEmailInUse(owner.getEmail())) {\n      return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n  }\n  ```\n- A new helper mirroring the style of `isTelephoneInUse`, comparing case-insensitively (lower-cased) against every existing owner's email:\n  ```java\n  private boolean isEmailInUse(String email) {\n      String normalized = email.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);\n      return this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n          .map(Owner::getEmail)\n          .filter(existing -> existing != null)\n          .map(existing -> existing.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT))\n          .anyMatch(normalized::equals);\n  }\n  ```\n\nOwners without an email are unaffected, and a second owner reusing an existing lower-cased email now gets a **409 Conflict**.\n\n## Test results\n- `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes.\n- Full suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
